#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-clone(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:7
msgid "git-clone - Clone a repository into a new directory"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:21
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"git clone [--template=<template-directory>]\n"
"\t  [-l] [-s] [--no-hardlinks] [-q] [-n] [--bare] [--mirror]\n"
"\t  [-o <name>] [-b <name>] [-u <upload-pack>] [--reference <repository>]\n"
"\t  [--dissociate] [--separate-git-dir <git-dir>]\n"
"\t  [--depth <depth>] [--[no-]single-branch] [--no-tags]\n"
"\t  [--recurse-submodules[=<pathspec>]] [--[no-]shallow-submodules]\n"
"\t  [--[no-]remote-submodules] [--jobs <n>] [--sparse] "
"[--[no-]reject-shallow]\n"
"\t  [--filter=<filter-spec>] [--also-filter-submodules]] [--] <repository>\n"
"\t  [<directory>]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:23
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:30
msgid ""
"Clones a repository into a newly created directory, creates remote-tracking "
"branches for each branch in the cloned repository (visible using `git branch "
"--remotes`), and creates and checks out an initial branch that is forked "
"from the cloned repository's currently active branch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:36
msgid ""
"After the clone, a plain `git fetch` without arguments will update all the "
"remote-tracking branches, and a `git pull` without arguments will in "
"addition merge the remote master branch into the current master branch, if "
"any (this is untrue when `--single-branch` is given; see below)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:41
msgid ""
"This default configuration is achieved by creating references to the remote "
"branch heads under `refs/remotes/origin` and by initializing "
"`remote.origin.url` and `remote.origin.fetch` configuration variables."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:44
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:45
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-l`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:46
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--local`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:53
msgid ""
"When the repository to clone from is on a local machine, this flag bypasses "
"the normal \"Git aware\" transport mechanism and clones the repository by "
"making a copy of `HEAD` and everything under objects and refs directories.  "
"The files under `.git/objects/` directory are hardlinked to save space when "
"possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:60
msgid ""
"If the repository is specified as a local path (e.g., `/path/to/repo`), this "
"is the default, and `--local` is essentially a no-op.  If the repository is "
"specified as a URL, then this flag is ignored (and we never use the local "
"optimizations).  Specifying `--no-local` will override the default when "
"`/path/to/repo` is given, using the regular Git transport instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:65
msgid ""
"If the repository's `$GIT_DIR/objects` has symbolic links or is a symbolic "
"link, the clone will fail. This is a security measure to prevent the "
"unintentional copying of files by dereferencing the symbolic links."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:69
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*NOTE*: this operation can race with concurrent modification to the\n"
"source repository, similar to running `cp -r <src> <dst>` while modifying\n"
"_<src>_.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:70
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-hardlinks`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:75
msgid ""
"Force the cloning process from a repository on a local filesystem to copy "
"the files under the `.git/objects` directory instead of using "
"hardlinks. This may be desirable if you are trying to make a back-up of your "
"repository."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:76
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-s`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:77
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--shared`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:83
msgid ""
"When the repository to clone is on the local machine, instead of using hard "
"links, automatically setup `.git/objects/info/alternates` to share the "
"objects with the source repository.  The resulting repository starts out "
"without any object of its own."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:93
msgid ""
"this is a possibly dangerous operation; do *not* use it unless you "
"understand what it does. If you clone your repository using this option and "
"then delete branches (or use any other Git command that makes any existing "
"commit unreferenced) in the source repository, some objects may become "
"unreferenced (or dangling).  These objects may be removed by normal Git "
"operations (such as `git commit`)  which automatically call `git maintenance "
"run --auto`. (See linkgit:git-maintenance[1].) If these objects are removed "
"and were referenced by the cloned repository, then the cloned repository "
"will become corrupt."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:99
msgid ""
"Note that running `git repack` without the `--local` option in a repository "
"cloned with `--shared` will copy objects from the source repository into a "
"pack in the cloned repository, removing the disk space savings of `clone "
"--shared`.  It is safe, however, to run `git gc`, which uses the `--local` "
"option by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:103
msgid ""
"If you want to break the dependency of a repository cloned with `--shared` "
"on its source repository, you can simply run `git repack -a` to copy all "
"objects from the source repository into a pack in the cloned repository."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:104
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--reference[-if-able] <repository>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:114
msgid ""
"If the reference _<repository>_ is on the local machine, automatically setup "
"`.git/objects/info/alternates` to obtain objects from the reference "
"_<repository>_.  Using an already existing repository as an alternate will "
"require fewer objects to be copied from the repository being cloned, "
"reducing network and local storage costs.  When using the "
"`--reference-if-able`, a non existing directory is skipped with a warning "
"instead of aborting the clone."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:117
msgid "see the NOTE for the `--shared` option, and also the `--dissociate` option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:118
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--dissociate`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:128
msgid ""
"Borrow the objects from reference repositories specified with the "
"`--reference` options only to reduce network transfer, and stop borrowing "
"from them after a clone is made by making necessary local copies of borrowed "
"objects.  This option can also be used when cloning locally from a "
"repository that already borrows objects from another repository--the new "
"repository will borrow objects from the same repository, and this option can "
"be used to stop the borrowing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:129
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-q`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:130
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--quiet`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:133
msgid "Operate quietly.  Progress is not reported to the standard error stream."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:134
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-v`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:135
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--verbose`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:138
msgid ""
"Run verbosely. Does not affect the reporting of progress status to the "
"standard error stream."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:139
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--progress`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:144
msgid ""
"Progress status is reported on the standard error stream by default when it "
"is attached to a terminal, unless `--quiet` is specified. This flag forces "
"progress status even if the standard error stream is not directed to a "
"terminal."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:145
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--server-option=<option>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:155
msgid ""
"Transmit the given string to the server when communicating using protocol "
"version 2.  The given string must not contain a NUL or LF character.  The "
"server's handling of server options, including unknown ones, is "
"server-specific.  When multiple `--server-option=<option>` are given, they "
"are all sent to the other side in the order listed on the command line.  "
"When no ++--server-option=++__<option>__ is given from the command line, the "
"values of configuration variable `remote.<name>.serverOption` are used "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:156
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-n`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:157
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-checkout`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:159
msgid "No checkout of `HEAD` is performed after the clone is complete."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:160
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--`[`no-`]`reject-shallow`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:164
msgid ""
"Fail if the source repository is a shallow repository.  The "
"`clone.rejectShallow` configuration variable can be used to specify the "
"default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:165
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--bare`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:176
msgid ""
"Make a 'bare' Git repository.  That is, instead of creating _<directory>_ "
"and placing the administrative files in `<directory>/.git`, make the "
"_<directory>_ itself the `$GIT_DIR`. This obviously implies the "
"`--no-checkout` because there is nowhere to check out the working tree.  "
"Also the branch heads at the remote are copied directly to corresponding "
"local branch heads, without mapping them to `refs/remotes/origin/`.  When "
"this option is used, neither remote-tracking branches nor the related "
"configuration variables are created."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:177
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--sparse`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:182
msgid ""
"Employ a sparse-checkout, with only files in the toplevel directory "
"initially being present.  The linkgit:git-sparse-checkout[1] command can be "
"used to grow the working directory as needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:183
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--filter=<filter-spec>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:192
msgid ""
"Use the partial clone feature and request that the server sends a subset of "
"reachable objects according to a given object filter.  When using "
"`--filter`, the supplied _<filter-spec>_ is used for the partial clone "
"filter. For example, `--filter=blob:none` will filter out all blobs (file "
"contents) until needed by Git. Also, `--filter=blob:limit=<size>` will "
"filter out all blobs of size at least _<size>_. For more details on filter "
"specifications, see the `--filter` option in linkgit:git-rev-list[1]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:193
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--also-filter-submodules`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:197
msgid ""
"Also apply the partial clone filter to any submodules in the repository.  "
"Requires `--filter` and `--recurse-submodules`. This can be turned on by "
"default by setting the `clone.filterSubmodules` config option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:198
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--mirror`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:205
msgid ""
"Set up a mirror of the source repository.  This implies `--bare`.  Compared "
"to `--bare`, `--mirror` not only maps local branches of the source to local "
"branches of the target, it maps all refs (including remote-tracking "
"branches, notes etc.) and sets up a refspec configuration such that all "
"these refs are overwritten by a `git remote update` in the target "
"repository."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:206
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-o` _<name>_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:207
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--origin` _<name>_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:211
msgid ""
"Instead of using the remote name `origin` to keep track of the upstream "
"repository, use _<name>_.  Overrides `clone.defaultRemoteName` from the "
"config."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:212
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-b` _<name>_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:213
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--branch` _<name>_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:220
msgid ""
"Instead of pointing the newly created `HEAD` to the branch pointed to by the "
"cloned repository's `HEAD`, point to _<name>_ branch instead. In a non-bare "
"repository, this is the branch that will be checked out.  `--branch` can "
"also take tags and detaches the `HEAD` at that commit in the resulting "
"repository."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:221
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-u` _<upload-pack>_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:222
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--upload-pack` _<upload-pack>_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:226
msgid ""
"When given, and the repository to clone from is accessed via ssh, this "
"specifies a non-default path for the command run on the other end."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:227
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--template=<template-directory>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:230
msgid ""
"Specify the directory from which templates will be used; (See the \"TEMPLATE "
"DIRECTORY\" section of linkgit:git-init[1].)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:231
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-c` `<key>=<value>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:232
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--config` `<key>=<value>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:241
msgid ""
"Set a configuration variable in the newly-created repository; this takes "
"effect immediately after the repository is initialized, but before the "
"remote history is fetched or any files checked out.  The _<key>_ is in the "
"same format as expected by linkgit:git-config[1] (e.g., `core.eol=true`). If "
"multiple values are given for the same key, each value will be written to "
"the config file. This makes it safe, for example, to add additional fetch "
"refspecs to the origin remote."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:247
msgid ""
"Due to limitations of the current implementation, some configuration "
"variables do not take effect until after the initial fetch and checkout.  "
"Configuration variables known to not take effect are: `remote.<name>.mirror` "
"and `remote.<name>.tagOpt`.  Use the corresponding `--mirror` and "
"`--no-tags` options instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:248
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--depth <depth>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:254
msgid ""
"Create a 'shallow' clone with a history truncated to the specified number of "
"commits. Implies `--single-branch` unless `--no-single-branch` is given to "
"fetch the histories near the tips of all branches. If you want to clone "
"submodules shallowly, also pass `--shallow-submodules`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:255
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--shallow-since=<date>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:257
msgid "Create a shallow clone with a history after the specified time."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:258
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--shallow-exclude=<ref>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:262
msgid ""
"Create a shallow clone with a history, excluding commits reachable from a "
"specified remote branch or tag.  This option can be specified multiple "
"times."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:263
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--[no-]single-branch`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:272
msgid ""
"Clone only the history leading to the tip of a single branch, either "
"specified by the `--branch` option or the primary branch remote's `HEAD` "
"points at.  Further fetches into the resulting repository will only update "
"the remote-tracking branch for the branch this option was used for the "
"initial cloning.  If the `HEAD` at the remote did not point at any branch "
"when `--single-branch` clone was made, no remote-tracking branch is created."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:273
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-tags`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:279
msgid ""
"Don't clone any tags, and set `remote.<remote>.tagOpt=--no-tags` in the "
"config, ensuring that future `git pull` and `git fetch` operations won't "
"follow any tags. Subsequent explicit tag fetches will still work, (see "
"linkgit:git-fetch[1])."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:284
msgid ""
"Can be used in conjunction with `--single-branch` to clone and maintain a "
"branch with no references other than a single cloned branch. This is useful "
"e.g. to maintain minimal clones of the default branch of some repository for "
"search indexing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:285
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--recurse-submodules[=<pathspec>]`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:293
msgid ""
"After the clone is created, initialize and clone submodules within based on "
"the provided _<pathspec>_.  If no `=<pathspec>` is provided, all submodules "
"are initialized and cloned.  This option can be given multiple times for "
"pathspecs consisting of multiple entries.  The resulting clone has "
"`submodule.active` set to the provided pathspec, or \"`.`\" (meaning all "
"submodules) if no pathspec is provided."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:300
msgid ""
"Submodules are initialized and cloned using their default settings. This is "
"equivalent to running `git submodule update --init --recursive <pathspec>` "
"immediately after the clone is finished. This option is ignored if the "
"cloned repository does not have a worktree/checkout (i.e. if any of "
"`--no-checkout`/`-n`, `--bare`, or `--mirror` is given)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:301
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--[no-]shallow-submodules`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:303
msgid "All submodules which are cloned will be shallow with a depth of 1."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:304
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--[no-]remote-submodules`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:309
msgid ""
"All submodules which are cloned will use the status of the submodule's "
"remote-tracking branch to update the submodule, rather than the "
"superproject's recorded SHA-1. Equivalent to passing `--remote` to `git "
"submodule update`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:310
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--separate-git-dir=<git-dir>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:316
msgid ""
"Instead of placing the cloned repository where it is supposed to be, place "
"the cloned repository at the specified directory, then make a "
"filesystem-agnostic Git symbolic link to there.  The result is Git "
"repository can be separated from working tree."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:317
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--ref-format=<ref-format>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:320
msgid ""
"Specify the given ref storage format for the repository. The valid values "
"are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:323
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-j` _<n>_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:324
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--jobs` _<n>_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:327
msgid ""
"The number of submodules fetched at the same time.  Defaults to the "
"`submodule.fetchJobs` option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:328
#, no-wrap
msgid "_<repository>_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:332
msgid ""
"The (possibly remote) _<repository>_ to clone from.  See the <<URLS,GIT "
"URLS>> section below for more information on specifying repositories."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:333
#, no-wrap
msgid "_<directory>_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:339
msgid ""
"The name of a new directory to clone into.  The \"humanish\" part of the "
"source repository is used if no _<directory>_ is explicitly given (`repo` "
"for `/path/to/repo.git` and `foo` for `host.xz:foo/.git`).  Cloning into an "
"existing directory is only allowed if the directory is empty."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:340
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--bundle-uri=<uri>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:346
msgid ""
"Before fetching from the remote, fetch a bundle from the given _<uri>_ and "
"unbundle the data into the local repository. The refs in the bundle will be "
"stored under the hidden `refs/bundle/*` namespace. This option is "
"incompatible with `--depth`, `--shallow-since`, and `--shallow-exclude`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:351
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXAMPLES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:354
msgid "Clone from upstream:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:359
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git clone git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/.../linux.git my-linux\n"
"$ cd my-linux\n"
"$ make\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:363
msgid ""
"Make a local clone that borrows from the current directory, without checking "
"things out:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:368
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git clone -l -s -n . ../copy\n"
"$ cd ../copy\n"
"$ git show-branch\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:372
msgid "Clone from upstream while borrowing from an existing local directory:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:378
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git clone --reference /git/linux.git \\\n"
"\tgit://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/.../linux.git \\\n"
"\tmy-linux\n"
"$ cd my-linux\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-clone.txt:382
msgid "Create a bare repository to publish your changes to the public:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
